"""Formula catalogue tied to the actual calculation stages."""
FORMULAS = [
('Universe and samples',r'\mathcal U_t=\{i:\operatorname{cap}_{i,t}\ge 2\times10^9,\ \operatorname{complete}_{i,t}(2520)=1\}',
 'Current NYSE/Nasdaq listings and current market capitalisation; US domicile and security-type screens. Mandatory complete positive finite prices across the last 2520 completed sessions before ANY horizon test. Historical point-in-time membership is not reconstructed. One eligible share class per issuer.'),
('Complete-case sample',r'\mathcal U_H=\{i:\forall t\in\mathcal T_H,\ P_{i,t}\in\mathbb R,\ 0<P_{i,t}<\infty\}',
 'The last 2520 officially completed exchange sessions define the common calendar. A single missing, nonfinite or nonpositive observation rejects the ticker from ALL horizons. No forward fill, backfill, interpolation or horizon-specific readmission.'),
('Daily log returns and standardisation',r'r_{i,t}=\log P_{i,t}-\log P_{i,t-1},\quad z_{i,t}=\frac{r_{i,t}-\bar r_i}{\sqrt{T^{-1}\sum_t(r_{i,t}-\bar r_i)^2}}',
 'Adjusted close is used for research; StandardScaler uses population variance. Constant series are removed before correlation and discovery.'),
('Correlation prefilter',r'\rho_{ij}=T^{-1}z_i^\top z_j,\quad |\rho_{ij}|\ge0.30',
 'At most 60 peers, excluding the target itself. This screens candidates; it does not establish cointegration.'),
('LASSO candidate discovery',r'\widehat b_\alpha=\arg\min_b\left\{\frac{\|y-Xb\|_2^2}{2T}+\alpha\|b\|_1\right\},\quad\alpha_{\max}=T^{-1}\|X^\top y\|_\infty',
 '32 alpha ratios from 0.75 to 0.005; no intercept after standardisation; choose sparsest passing 2–5 peers with in-sample R² ≥ 0.70, then higher R². This is not out-of-sample validation.'),
('Candidate cleanup and fit',r'R^2=1-\frac{\sum_t(y_t-\widehat y_t)^2}{\sum_t(y_t-\bar y)^2},\quad |b_j|/\max_k|b_k|\ge0.01',
 'One canonical basket per horizon. R² is the original candidate fit before pruning and is not a fitted cointegration score.'),
('Johansen rank tests',r'J_{\rm trace}(r)=-T\sum_{j=r+1}^{n}\log(1-\widehat\lambda_j),\quad J_{\max}(r)=-T\log(1-\widehat\lambda_{r+1})',
 'Sequential rank decisions stop at the first non-rejection using 95% critical values. Confirmed rank is the smaller of trace and maximum-eigenvalue ranks. Require 0 < rank < basket size.'),
('BIC lag selection and sensitivity',r'\operatorname{BIC}(k)=\log|\widehat\Omega_k|+\frac{\log T}{T}d_k',
 'statsmodels VECM select_order, up to 10 lagged differences; constant specification co for lag selection. Re-test Johansen det_order 0 (constant) and −1 (none) at that lag; require matching reduced ranks. No multiple-testing adjustment is applied.'),
('Stationary spread coordinates',r'y_t=\log P_t,\quad x_t=B^\top y_t,\quad \|B_{\cdot j}\|_2=1',
 'Columns of B are selected Johansen eigenvectors with deterministic sign orientation. The entire stationary subspace is fitted jointly.'),
('Joint VAR(1) fit',r'x_{t+1}=c+Ax_t+\varepsilon_{t+1},\quad (\widehat c,\widehat A)=\arg\min_{c,A}\sum_t\|x_{t+1}-c-Ax_t\|_2^2',
 'OLS with an intercept. At least 100 observations; reject spectral radius ≥ 1−10⁻⁸ and ill-conditioned equilibrium/covariance. Innovation covariance uses ddof=1 and is not degrees-of-freedom adjusted for every regression parameter.'),
('Equilibrium and stationary covariance',r'\mu=(I-A)^{-1}c,\quad Q=\operatorname{Cov}(\widehat\varepsilon),\quad\Sigma=A\Sigma A^\top+Q',
 'Solve the discrete Lyapunov equation. Require positive definite Σ and condition numbers ≤ 10¹⁰.'),
('Marginal z-score and joint distance',r'd_t=x_t-\mu,\quad z_{j,t}=\frac{d_{j,t}}{\sqrt{\Sigma_{jj}}},\quad D_t=\sqrt{d_t^\top\Sigma^{-1}d_t}',
 'Joint distance is non-negative. D=|z| only for one component; multi-component distance is not a univariate sigma score or a guaranteed opportunity.'),
('Signal direction and weights',r's_t=-\Sigma^{-1}d_t,\quad a_t=Bs_t,\quad w_{i,t}=\frac{a_{i,t}}{\sum_j|a_{j,t}|}',
 'A covariance-scaled deviation heuristic. It is not the expected OU drift A−I and is not a demonstrated optimal trading allocation. Neither zero beta nor zero net dollar exposure is imposed.'),
('Research quantities and exposures',r'q_i=\frac{w_i}{P^{\rm adj}_{i,t}},\quad G=100\sum_i|w_i|,\quad N=100\sum_i w_i',
 'q represents adjusted-price research units per $1 gross exposure. Live shares require current executable, unadjusted broker quotes plus borrow and rounding checks.'),
('Market proxy and portfolio risk',r'm_t=\frac1{n_H}\sum_i r_{i,t},\quad r_{p,t}=\sum_i w_i r_{i,t},\quad\beta_p=\frac{\operatorname{Cov}(r_p,m)}{\operatorname{Var}(m)},\quad R_m^2=\operatorname{Corr}(r_p,m)^2',
 'Equal-weighted eligible-universe log-return proxy for each horizon, not SPY beta. Historical constant-weight log-return approximation; net and beta exposures are displayed, not neutralised.'),
('Continuous-time representation',r'K=-\log(A),\quad dx=K(\mu-x)\,dt+C\,dW_t',
 'One trading session per time unit. A real matrix logarithm alone is insufficient to certify continuous-time OU embeddability; implied diffusion CCᵀ=KΣ+ΣKᵀ must also be positive semidefinite.'),
('Modal convergence',r'h_j=\frac{\log(0.5)}{\log|\lambda_j(A)|},\quad g_j(u)=|\lambda_j(A)|^u',
 'Envelope half-life only for 0<|λ|<1. Complex modes may oscillate. A zero eigenvalue has immediate one-step decay. This is not a stock-return forecast.'),
('Rolling component diagnostics',r'\widehat\phi,\widehat b=\operatorname{OLS}(x_{t+1}\sim x_t),\quad\mu_r=\frac{\widehat b}{1-\widehat\phi},\quad\sigma_r=\frac{\operatorname{sd}(e)}{\sqrt{1-\widehat\phi^2}},\quad h_r=\frac{\log(0.5)}{\log\widehat\phi}',
 'Scalar AR(1) diagnostics on fixed fitted components: 252-session maximum window, 126-session minimum, every 21 sessions. They do not replace the joint MVOU model.'),
('Rolling drift and dispersion',r'\delta_r=\frac{|\mu_r-\mu|}{\sqrt{\Sigma_{jj}}},\quad v_r=\frac{\sigma_r}{\sqrt{\Sigma_{jj}}}',
 'ADF with constant and AIC lag choice. FLAGGED for missing diagnostics, invalid φ, p>0.10, δ>1.5 or v>2. RELIABLE for p≤0.05, δ≤1 and v≤1.5; otherwise WATCH. Heuristic labels, not probabilities.'),
('Historical rendering and training check',r't_{\rm split}=\lfloor0.8T\rfloor,\quad z_{j,t}^{\rm plotted}=\frac{B_{\cdot j}^{\top}\log P_t-\mu_j}{\sqrt{\Sigma_{jj}}}',
 'The rank check uses the first 80% of rows but full-sample basket selection and lag choice. Plots use full-sample B, μ and Σ at all historical dates. They are retrospective in-sample diagnostics, not walk-forward results.'),
]

FORMULAS += [
('Rolling trading-year clock',r'\mathcal T_t^{10}=\{s_{n-2519},\ldots,s_n\},\quad s_n=\max\{s:\operatorname{close}_{NYSE}(s)\le t\},\quad 10\times252=2520',
 'Ten trading years means exactly 2520 completed exchange sessions, recalculated from the run time; no fixed start date. Holidays and early closes come from the exchange calendar.'),
('Hard global eligibility gate',r'E_{i,t}=\mathbf 1\!\left[\forall s\in\mathcal T_t^{10}:P_{i,s}\in(0,\infty),\ P_{i,s}\ne\mathrm{NA};\ \text{dates unique}\right]',
 'Missing sessions are identified by reindexing against the official calendar, not by counting available rows. Any failure removes the ticker before discovery, all statistical tests and every horizon.'),
('Horizon slicing after eligibility',r'\mathcal U_t^H=\{i:E_{i,t}=1\},\quad |\mathcal T^H|=252H,\quad H\in\{1,3,5,10\}',
 'All horizons contain identical eligible tickers. FULL is the complete rolling 2520-session window. Shorter windows use the last 252, 756 or 1260 sessions, never a separate eligibility screen.'),
('Normalisation and orientation of vectors',r'\widetilde b_j=\frac{b_j}{\|b_j\|_2},\quad k=\arg\max_i|\widetilde b_{ij}|,\quad B_{\cdot j}=\operatorname{sign}(\widetilde b_{kj})\widetilde b_j',
 'Vectors are unit Euclidean norm; the largest absolute coefficient is positive. Coefficients are recorded in the exact ticker order used to construct the spread.'),
('Explicit OLS matrix solution',r'D=[\mathbf 1,X_{0:T-1}],\quad\widehat\Theta=D^+X_{1:T},\quad c=\widehat\Theta_{0,:}^{\top},\quad A=\widehat\Theta_{1:,:}^{\top}',
 'numpy least-squares solution. The transpose is required because observations are rows in code, whereas the mathematical VAR uses column state vectors.'),
('Innovation covariance estimator',r'e_t=x_{t+1}-c-Ax_t,\quad Q=\frac{1}{N-1}\sum_{t=1}^{N}(e_t-\bar e)(e_t-\bar e)^\top',
 'N is the number of lagged pairs. This is the implemented ddof=1 covariance; it is not the full parameter-count degrees-of-freedom adjustment.'),
('Stability and numerical conditioning',r'\rho(A)=\max_j|\lambda_j(A)|<1-10^{-8},\quad\kappa_2(M)=\frac{\sigma_{\max}(M)}{\sigma_{\min}(M)}\le10^{10},\quad M\in\{I-A,\Sigma\}',
 'Require positive eigenvalues of symmetrised Σ. Models that fail are not assigned normal computed-signal status.'),
('Continuous OU diffusion check',r'V=K\Sigma+\Sigma K^\top,\quad V=CC^\top\succeq0,\quad K=-\log A',
 'A real matrix logarithm and a positive-semidefinite implied diffusion are both required. Otherwise retain only the discrete representation; tolerance scales with matrix norm.'),
('Conditional OU mean movement',r'\mathbb E[x_{t+h}-\mu\mid x_t]=A^h(x_t-\mu),\quad\mathbb E[x_{t+1}-x_t\mid x_t]=(A-I)(x_t-\mu)',
 'Model implication documented to distinguish expected drift from the actual covariance-scaled deviation trading heuristic. The screener does not substitute this drift for its implemented signal.'),
('ADF regression and test statistic',r'\Delta x_t=\alpha+\gamma x_{t-1}+\sum_{j=1}^{p}\psi_j\Delta x_{t-j}+u_t,\quad\tau=\widehat\gamma/\operatorname{se}(\widehat\gamma)',
 'Null γ=0. statsmodels adfuller uses a constant, selects p by AIC and returns a nonstandard Dickey–Fuller p-value, not a normal-distribution p-value.'),
('Rolling reliability classification',r'\mathcal R=\begin{cases}\mathrm{FLAGGED}&\text{missing diagnostic, invalid }\phi,\ p>0.10,\ \delta>1.5\text{ or }v>2\\\mathrm{RELIABLE}&p\le0.05,\ \delta\le1,\ v\le1.5\\\mathrm{WATCH}&\text{otherwise}\end{cases}',
 'This piecewise rule is applied only after verifying all inputs are finite. It is a diagnostic label, not a calibrated probability or a live-trading pass.'),
('Training rank robustness',r'R_{\rm train}=\mathbf 1[0<r_0=r_{-1}<n],\quad T_{\rm train}=\lfloor0.8T\rfloor',
 'Ranks are tested sequentially on the first 80% of observations using the previously selected lag. Full-sample basket/lag selection prevents interpreting this as independent holdout validation.'),
('Portfolio and stock beta decomposition',r'\beta_i=\frac{\operatorname{Cov}(r_i,m)}{\operatorname{Var}(m)},\quad\beta_p=\sum_iw_i\beta_i,\quad R_m^2=\frac{\operatorname{Cov}(r_p,m)^2}{\operatorname{Var}(r_p)\operatorname{Var}(m)}',
 'Covariance and variance use the same aligned observations and ddof=1. The reported market-explained variance is 100R²; no beta neutrality is enforced.'),
]
